# Repo studio (universal interface)

Load `.agent-context.json` from the repo root (fall back to `.agent-context.local.json` for per-dev overrides). If neither exists, run `steps-pattern bootstrap-context` before answering architecture, deployment, or AWS questions.

Rules below apply to repos where `${repo.layout}` is set. Common layouts:
- `holding-repo-multi-product` — multiple product trees under `${repo.productsDir}/`, shared kits under `${repo.packagesDir}/`, each product owns its own lockfile and SST deploy root.
- `single-product` — one product at the repo root; `${repo.productsDir}` and `${repo.packagesDir}` may be empty.
- `monorepo-single-lockfile` — root-level `pnpm-workspace.yaml` or equivalent; different operational rules.

## Layout

- Shared kits: `${repo.packagesDir}/` (reused across products).
- Products: enumerate `${products[]}`. Each product root is `${repo.productsDir}/${products[i].slug}/` and may own:
  - its own lockfile (do not invent a repo-root lockfile for `holding-repo-multi-product`)
  - its own SST deploy root and stages
  - its own `.cursor/rules/` and `.cursor/skills/` under `${repo.productsDir}/${products[i].slug}/.cursor/`
- Repo-level tooling (if any): `${repo.toolsDir}` (optional; omit when unset).
- Active feature campaigns: `${repo.workDir}/<product>/<feature>/` (optional).

Run product-level `pnpm` / `sst` / migration commands from inside `${repo.productsDir}/${slug}/`, never from the repo root (when the layout is `holding-repo-multi-product`).

## AWS accounts

Skip this section if `${aws}` is unset (not every repo deploys to AWS).

- Organization: `${aws.organizationId}` managed from account `${aws.managementAccountId}`.
- OUs: `${aws.ous.deployments}` (product prod accounts) and `${aws.ous.sandboxes}` (personal/sandbox accounts) when both exist.
- Enumerate accounts from `${aws.accounts[]}` — each entry has `{ name, id, profile, product, stage, removalPolicy? }`.
- Closed/suspended accounts live in `${aws.closedAccounts[]}` and MUST NOT be redeployed to.
- Never deploy product A into product B's accounts.
- Never reuse another product's OIDC deploy role, product-prefixed GitHub secrets (`*_DOMAIN`, `*_ROLE_ARN`), or Roles-Anywhere trust anchors.
- Reuse the org pattern (OIDC, `remove` vs `retain`, personal-stage local Postgres); do not share account IDs or stacks.

### Account summary

For each `${aws.accounts[i]}`:
- Product: `${aws.accounts[i].product}` | Stage: `${aws.accounts[i].stage}` | Account: `${aws.accounts[i].id}` | AWS profile: `${aws.accounts[i].profile}` | Removal: `${aws.accounts[i].removalPolicy}` (if set).

## Domains

Skip this section if `${products[*].domains}` is empty.

Hosted zones live in the product's prod account, not in the registrar/management account. For each product with domains:
- `${products[i].slug}`: domains `${products[i].domains[].apex}` with zone IDs `${products[i].domains[].zoneId}`. Any entry with `role: "redirect-to-<slug>"` is an S3 website redirect + CloudFront + ACM, not a primary site.

## Guardrails

- If a product's `${products[i].sstGuard}` is set, that function MUST refuse non-matching account IDs and refuse closed stages (see `${aws.closedAccounts[]}`).
- A `.github/workflows/deploy-<slug>.yml` must assume `arn:aws:iam::<accountId>:role/<oidcRole>` scoped to `repo:<owner>/<repo>:environment:<githubEnvironment>` from `${aws.accounts[]}`.
- Push to `main` deploys production only for products whose `${products[i].branchDeploy}` is `main`.
